.TH SLKD 8 "2026-10-16" "SparkLink development" "System Manager's Manual"
.SH NAME
slkd \- per-controller SparkLink management and application service daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B slkd
.RB [ \-c " " path ]
.RB [ \-d " " path ]
.RB [ \-n ]
.RB [ \-\-storage " " directory ]
.RB [ \-\-session ]
.br
.B slkd \-\-config
.I path
.B \-\-check-config
.RB [ \-\-dump-ws73-policies ]
.SH SCOPE
This manual describes unreleased userspace source 8121ba0fc038 and matching
Linux 8cbf53e6a088. Interfaces may change without compatibility retention.
Current qualification is recorded separately in
.I project/current-capabilities.md
and its structured provenance records. An exposed method name is not a
hardware capability. All experimental drivers and real WS73 operations must
run inside the prepared VM; building documentation does not operate devices.
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B slkd
watches controller registrations through
.I /dev/sparklink
and publishes the system-bus name
.BR org.sparklink .
Each controller has its own generation-bound state and management ownership.
Installed, Ready, connected, channel-negotiated, policy-approved,
controller-reported encryption and authenticated identity are distinct states.
Replugging or reconnecting does not restore an old object's authority.
.PP
Native applications receive authorized logical-channel socket fds through
Connection objects. SSAP uses the unique userspace Engine on that channel;
the removed kernel SSAP database and wire facade are not fallback paths.
Transport submission or NOCP is not proof of peer application processing.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-c " path" ", \-\-config " path
Explicit TOML configuration. A missing, unreadable, invalid or unsupported
explicit configuration aborts startup before bus registration or management.
Only a missing implicit /etc/sparklink/main.conf permits built-in defaults.
.TP
.B \-\-check-config
Requires --config. Validate with the production parser and exit before
D-Bus or controller startup. Success validates host policy, not firmware support.
.TP
.B \-\-dump-ws73-policies
Requires --check-config. Print normalized WS73 policy diagnostics.
.TP
.BI \-d " path" ", \-\-device " path
Kernel character device; default /dev/sparklink.
.TP
.BI \-\-storage " directory"
Metadata store root; default /var/lib/sparklink. Legacy metadata is not a
trusted key store, native Bond implementation or authenticated credential.
.TP
.B \-\-session
Use a session bus for isolated tests. Does not reproduce deployed system-bus
policy or grant kernel permissions.
.TP
.B \-n, \-\-nodetach
Accepted foreground option. The current daemon has no detach/fork path.
.SH OBJECTS AND INTERFACES
The root /org/sparklink exposes org.sparklink.Manager:
Version() returns s; ListRegistrations() and ListAdapters() return as.
Registration observation and Ready adapters are not interchangeable.
.PP
Adapter paths are /org/sparklink/slk{index}_g{generation}, not stable
/adapterN or /slk0 aliases. Obtain actual paths from the manager.
org.sparklink.Adapter provides generation-bound observation, discovery
requests/results and connection enumeration. Management requests are
asynchronous; admission does not indicate radio completion.
.PP
Canonical peers are below /peer_t{type}_{address}; physical Connection
objects append /link_{lifetime}. org.sparklink.Connection.GetInfo() returns
(ttqyy sbb) as one structure (spaces shown only for readability): generation,
lifetime, handle, role, address type, address, known, connected.
OpenChannel() and OpenChannelScoped() return a D-Bus Unix fd (h), subject to
native identity, grant, scope and mode checks. Closing one's channel does not
mean stopping the controller. Old fd, handle or address cannot select a new lifetime.
.SS Explicit limited security
org.sparklink.Security is at the adapter's /security child.
RegisterAgent(o path, s method) and UnregisterAgent(o path) manage one explicit
Agent unique bus owner for that controller. Methods are sdk111-no-mitm and
sdk111-numeric-comparison; no fallback or automatic approval. The original
Agent epoch and method are frozen at allocation. Numeric mode first requests
authorization to start, then ConfirmNumericComparison with the original prompt
and live u32 code. False rejects; timeout/loss cancels only the original request.
A started native ioctl is joined before cleanup; no controller release or
physical-debt erasure is implied. Trusted Grant, Bond and global Pair remain
unsupported.
.PP
On org.sparklink.Connection, AllocateReferenceSecurity(u timeout_ms) returns
a caller-bound t request_id. The original 1-5000 ms CLOCK_MONOTONIC deadline
starts at allocation, before Agent waiting. BeginReferenceSecurity(t id,
s method) starts the asynchronous operation. GetReferenceSecurityResult(t id)
returns separate policy/native observations. CancelReferenceSecurity(t id)
returns a withdrawal-request boolean, not hardware cleanup acknowledgement.
.PP
The Agent implements org.sparklink.Agent.AuthorizeReferenceSecurity with one
structure argument (stttqyy sst), containing connection path, request id,
generation, lifetime, handle, role, address type, address, method and original
deadline in monotonic nanoseconds, and returns b. Spaces are not part of the
D-Bus signature. Policy approval does not authenticate the peer or install a Bond.
.PP
SDK111-specific unauthenticated key agreement/installation has narrowly
qualified two-device evidence. Generic Pair(s), Encrypt(), GetInfo(), SetPsk(s),
passkey methods, Reset(), and Encrypted/Paired properties remain NotSupported;
invalid arguments may be rejected first. ListBonded()/RemoveBond(s) operate
legacy local metadata only and do not establish or revoke real trusted keys.
.SS Local service data and remote SSAP
org.sparklink.ServiceManager is at /services.
RegisterLocalService(ay uuid, a(ayuuay) properties) returns (qqaq): service
start, end and property handles. UUIDs are nonzero 2 or 16-byte values;
properties contain UUID, operations, access requirements and initial value.
Access mask 0x3f is separate from operation bits; encryption bits 1/8 and
numeric-comparison mechanism bits 2/16 govern write/read respectively.
Local-authorization bits 4/32 remain NotSupported; reserved bits are InvalidArgs. Current operations
are READ=1 and WRITE_WITH_RSP=4. Limits are 16 services, 64 properties,
2042 bytes per value and 8192 aggregate value bytes per registration.
ListLocalServices() returns a(qqaya(qayuu)); RemoveLocalService(q start) and
ReadLocalValue(q handle) operate the local database. Local registration
success is not remote service-discovery or publication success.
.PP
The old RegisterServices(), AddService(q,b), AddProperty(q,y,ay),
ReadProperty(q), WriteProperty(q,ay), Notify(q) and other legacy facade
methods remain NotSupported (InvalidArgs may precede it). In particular,
RegisterServices takes no JSON argument and Notify takes no value argument.
The old org.sparklink.RemoteService facade is unsupported. Actual limited
remote exchange/discovery/read/write uses the Connection SSAP actor.
Notification/indication, long write and full Profile delivery are not promised.
.SS Remaining interfaces
Controller and ExtAdv names do not imply support for legacy PHY, RPA,
measurement, PM or extended-advertising controls. Unsupported methods fail
explicitly. See the website's interface reference and current qualification;
the complete field/error reference remains under documentation remediation.
.SH PERMISSIONS AND FAILURES
System-bus policy distinguishes ordinary applications (sparklink-apps),
controller administration (sparklink), observation and Agent operations.
The policy file and native kernel authorization both apply; access to a bus
method does not grant CAP_NET_ADMIN or controller ownership. A received fd
retains its scope and revocation rules, not the sender's general privileges.
.PP
AccessDenied, InvalidArgs, NotSupported and Failed have distinct meanings.
A stale generation/lifetime, missing Agent, expired original deadline,
revocation, queue exhaustion or disconnect is not silent success.
Do not retry with a new identity or renewed deadline as if it were the same request.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/sparklink/main.conf
Configuration; see sparklink.conf(5) and the single WS73 policy reference.
.TP
.I /dev/sparklink
Native kernel interface; permissions and experimental VM setup are required.
.TP
.I /var/lib/sparklink/
Legacy metadata by default; no native trusted Bond persistence qualification.
.SH SIGNALS
SIGINT and SIGTERM request manager shutdown and per-controller cleanup.
Daemon restart does not promise survival of all application sockets.
.SH INSTALLATION LIMITS
Experimental bundles and generic installation are different paths. The generic
Makefile/service prefix mismatch, upgrade/rollback and uninstall preservation
remain tracked; this manual does not certify a clean-distribution deployment.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR slctl (1),
.BR sparklink.conf (5),
.BR dbus-daemon (1)

.PP
Connection ReadSsapValue(q handle,u minimum), WriteSsapValue(q handle,ay value,u minimum)
and ReadSsapByUuid(q start,q end,y data_type,ay uuid,u minimum) use mechanism
minimum 0..2 and the existing authorized SMTC fd. Initial requests and responses
carry restrictive per-send epoch and original deadline constraints. Preparing
an intent does not renew authorization or reserve credit. Numeric comparison
is not a named identity or Bond. Read denial error 8/10 and write denial leave
protected values undisclosed or unchanged; timeout after admitted write does
not imply rollback. Exact source/artifact qualification is separate.
